[size=6][b]SpaceBourne 2 Realism: installer and updater[/b][/size]

One window to install, switch on and update the whole SpaceBourne 2 realism mod set. Tick the mods you want, press [b]Apply ticks[/b], and play.

[list]
[*][b]Pick your mods.[/b] Every mod in the set is listed with a short description. Install all of them or just one.
[*][b]Ticked means on.[/b] Every ticked mod is installed [i]and[/i] switched on, even one that ships switched off on its own.
[*][b]See what's out of date.[/b] It shows the version you have and the newest release on GitHub. [b]Update all[/b] downloads and installs every newer version for you.
[*][b]Your settings stay.[/b] An update keeps every setting you changed in config.lua and gives the others the new release's defaults, so new tuning reaches you. The log lists the settings it kept. The defaults of your version are next to it as config.default.lua.
[*][b]Safe.[/b] It never touches your saves or the game's executable. Before it replaces or removes a mod, it keeps a backup in %LOCALAPPDATA%\SB2Realism\backups.
[*][b]UE4SS included.[/b] If UE4SS is missing, one click installs UE4SS 3.0.1, the version every mod in the set is built for.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]How to use[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download the zip from [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism/releases]Releases[/url] or Nexus, and extract it anywhere.
[*]Close SpaceBourne 2.
[*]Double-click [b]Install SB2 Realism.cmd[/b].
[*]The installer finds the game through Steam. For GOG or another location, press [b]Browse[/b] and pick the SpaceBourne 2 folder.
[*]Tick the mods you want and press [b]Apply ticks[/b].
[/list]

What the buttons do:

[list]
[*][b]Play[/b]: Starts SpaceBourne 2 (through Steam for Steam copies). When SB2 HOTAS is on, it starts its bridge app first.
[*][b]Apply ticks[/b]: Installs and switches on every ticked mod. Switches off every unticked mod; you choose whether its files are deleted (a backup is kept).
[*][b]Update all[/b]: Installs the newest release of every installed mod that has one.
[*][b]Check for updates[/b]: Asks GitHub for the newest versions. It also runs when the window opens, unless you untick that option.
[*][b]Open mod page[/b]: Opens the selected mod's Nexus page. Double-clicking a row does the same.
[*][b]Open SB2 HOTAS[/b]: Opens the SB2 HOTAS bridge app, which must run while you play. The first time, it offers to download it (about 50 MB).
[/list]

When Windows asks, allow the script to run. It is plain PowerShell, so you can read every line in SB2RealismInstaller.ps1.

[line]
[size=5][b]The realism set[/b][/size]

[b]HTR is the core, the rest are extras, and every mod also works alone.[/b] The set was designed around Hardcore Tactical Realism as the core mod, with each other mod adding one part of the realism collection on top of it. HTR is not required, though: every mod works on its own, in any combination. We tested all the extras together without HTR, in game and on foot, with no errors. Tick only what you want.

[list]
[*][b]Hardcore Tactical Realism (HTR)[/b]: Combat and AI overhaul: caliber vs armor, hit zones, wounds, faction doctrines (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Nexus[/url] · [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/1646850/discussions/0/573805072991123580/]Steam[/url])
[*][b]Split Controls[/b]: Separate look inversion for ships and on foot (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SplitControls]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/5]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Silent Ops[/b]: Realistic stealth, suppressors, silent takedowns (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SilentOps]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/6]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Gear Without Levels[/b]: Any weapon or suit at any level, with small penalties (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GearWithoutLevels]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/7]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]SB2 HOTAS[/b]: Joystick, HOTAS, pedals, head tracking, triple screen (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HOTAS]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/8]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Faction Power[/b]: Dungeons, sales and missions earn your faction power (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-FactionPower]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/9]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Tactical Engineering[/b]: Deployable turrets that take time to set up (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalEngineering]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/10]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Ammo Discipline[/b]: Realistic ammo limits and scavenging: every magazine counts (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-AmmoDiscipline]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/12]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Ground Waypoints[/b]: Planet waypoints on foot and on the hoverbike (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GroundWaypoints]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/13]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Get Out of the Way[/b]: NPCs step aside naturally when you walk through them (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GetOutOfTheWay]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/14]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Tactical First Person[/b]: First person on foot with weapons held up and aim down the sights (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalFirstPerson]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/15]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Clear HUD[/b]: A reticle you can see and HUD colours of your choice (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-ClearHUD]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/16]Nexus[/url])
[*][b]Bigger Armies[/b]: More general slots for your faction: twice the ground and space forces (Links: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/17]Nexus[/url])
[/list]

SB2 HOTAS has its own bridge app. When you tick it, the installer downloads the app to %LOCALAPPDATA%\SB2Realism\apps\hotas and runs its own install for the in-game part. [b]Update all[/b] keeps that copy up to date. Your controller setup is kept, because the bridge saves it in %LOCALAPPDATA%\SB2HOTAS. If you already use your own copy of the bridge, that's fine too: [b]Play[/b] notices it running.

[line]
[size=5][b]Details[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]On/off switch.[/b] A mod is switched on through its line in SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\mods.txt (Name : 1). Managed mods don't use enabled.txt, so switching a mod off really switches it off.
[*][b]Ticking a mod switches on its main features.[/b]
    - It sets the master switch in config.lua, e.g. Enabled (and StartOn for Tactical Engineering).
    - If the mod remembers an in-game toggle, it resets that toggle to on.
    - Optional extras inside a mod keep your choice, e.g. HTR's gear bonus.
[*][b]Choices at install.[/b] When you first install Clear HUD, a small window asks for the reticle colour and the HUD colour. Close it to keep the defaults. You can change them later in ClearHUD\scripts\config.lua.
[*][b]Command line[/b] (for scripts): `` powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File SB2RealismInstaller.ps1 -NoGui -List powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File SB2RealismInstaller.ps1 -NoGui -Apply "htr,silentops,gear" [-Delete] powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File SB2RealismInstaller.ps1 -NoGui -UpdateAll ` Mod ids are in mods.json. -GamePath "D:\Games\SpaceBourne 2"` skips the automatic search.
[/list]

